    | Non-cyclotomic ring AKS variant Z_n[x]/(x^d+a) (FOCUS-1 sub-attack 2) | FAIL | E+C | Builds (x+b)^n =? x^n + b in Z_n[x]/(x^d+a) at small d, replacing standard AKS modulus x^r-1. Empirical sweep d in {3..12}, a in {1,2}, n up to 410041 inc. 30 Carmichaels. Clean structural finding: cyclotomic-flavour (a=1) leaks Carmichaels at small d (19/30 at d=3, 5/30 at d=6, 3/30 at d=4 = Phi_8) — Carmichael Frobenius alignment with small cyclotomic factors of x^d+1; non-cyclotomic Eisenstein (a=2) leaks 0/30 at every d tested. (E) Even with a=2, evaluating the congruence requires polylog-dim matrix powering — exactly the growing-dim MPOW primitive (E5.3) that is the open Chain-E frontier; modulus structure is orthogonal to depth. (C) Capelli's theorem certifies x^d+a irreducible over F_p in TC^0, but requires p|n known — circular for primality testing on input n. No correctness theorem analog of AKS counting argument exists for Eisenstein moduli. Refines line 690 (S47 cyclotomic-CRT). Confirms FOCUS-1 sub-attack 2 closed; sub-attacks 1 (Bernstein 2003 smaller-r) and 3 (Healy-Viola Frobenius transplant) remain. See experiments/circuit_complexity/aks_alternative/non_cyclotomic_ring/. | 37 |
