    103	## 5. Bogomolny-Keating arithmetic-correction probe
    104	
    105	**Hypothesis to test:** D(s) = R_2_emp(s) - R_2_GUE(s) at the extended N
    106	has a prime-driven shape predicted by Bogomolny-Keating 1996:
    107	
    108	    D_BK(s; T) ≈ -(2/L²) ∑_{p, k≥1} [(log p)² / pᵏ]
    109	                                    · cos(2π s · k log p / L)
    110	
    111	where L = log(T_mean / 2π).  We Pearson-correlate the empirical D(s)
    112	with this multi-prime template (restricted to bulk s > 0.5 to avoid
    113	level-repulsion edge effects).  The CRITICAL caveat is that this
    114	Pearson is only meaningful in comparison to a properly matched null —
    115	see the gap-shuffled-null z-score below, not the raw value.
    116	
    117	| N | Pearson(D_emp, D_BK) | |D_emp|_max | |D_BK_pred|_max | L = log(T_mean/2π) |
    118	|---|----------------------|-------------|------------------|---------------------|
    119	| 2000 | +0.101 | 0.273 | 0.2847 | 5.305 |
    120	| 8000 | +0.111 | 0.206 | 0.1909 | 6.476 |
    121	
    122	**Marginal correlation (+0.111) — suggestive but not conclusive.**
    123	Could be coincidental given many-prime template; not novel without
